From: ExposureMG <exposuremg@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:32:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] meson: allow panvk on Windows with a libdrm-compatible
 library

On Windows, panvk reaches a panthor-compatible kernel driver through a
libdrm-compatible library (render-node ioctls and syncobjs, no KMS), so
look libdrm up there when panvk is enabled.

Also build with -mno-ms-bitfields with MinGW when panfrost is enabled: the
panfrost compiler static-asserts the size of structs with mixed-type
bitfields, which only holds with the GCC layout, and those structs are
shared with NIR/util, so the flag is applied project-wide.

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 meson.build | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index c1d17bc..9e7be78 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -812,6 +812,10 @@ if system_has_kms_drm
       'amdgpu' : _libdrm_checks['amdgpu']['enabled'].to_string('enabled', 'disabled'),
     },
   )
+elif host_machine.system() == 'windows' and with_panfrost_vk
+  # On Windows, panvk talks to a panthor-compatible kernel driver through a
+  # libdrm-compatible library (render-node ioctls and syncobjs, no KMS).
+  dep_libdrm = dependency('libdrm', version : '>=' + _drm_ver)
 else
   # We should prevent libdrm from being available when the target doesn't have it to avoid transitive
   # dependencies (such as vk-runtime) linking to it
@@ -1336,6 +1340,14 @@ elif host_machine.system() == 'windows'
     # MINGW also accept _GNU_SOURCE
     pre_args += '-D_GNU_SOURCE'
 
+    # The panfrost compiler static-asserts the size of structs with mixed-type
+    # bitfields, which only holds with the GCC/Itanium layout. Apply it to
+    # everything so that structs shared with NIR, util and the Vulkan runtime
+    # have one layout.
+    if with_panfrost_vk or with_gallium_panfrost
+      pre_args += '-mno-ms-bitfields'
+    endif
+
     # When the target is not (mingw with ucrt)
     # NOTE: clang's stddef.h are conflict with mingw or ucrt's stddef.h
     # So do not include headers that defined in clang for detecting
